# =========================================================================
# orch.bcyr — benchmarks for the orchestration group.
#
# No oracle bench file: rust-old/benches/ has no orchestrator.rs. These measure
# what a crew run actually hammers — the event fan-out on every task boundary,
# the per-task ranking and delegation, the DAG sort, the plan-cache key, and the
# conversation trim that runs on every push.
#
# **Fan-out is measured as a round trip.** A subscriber's ring is 256 deep, so a
# send-only loop saturates it after 256 iterations and then measures nothing but
# the eviction path. Draining inside the loop keeps the reader in step and gives
# the number a real deployment sees. `event_send_evicting` measures the other
# case deliberately, against a ring left full on purpose: that is the cost of
# the overwrite-oldest guarantee blocker #4 was about, and the number worth
# knowing is that a stalled SSE client does not get more expensive to serve.
#
# **Logging is turned down to SK_FATAL.** `agnosai_delegate_tasks` emits an INFO
# line per call, matching the oracle's `info!`, and `orch_pubsub` and the event
# bus log on their rejection paths. Left at the default level a delegation
# benchmark measures sakshi writing to a pipe, not the delegation. The log cost
# is real in production and is worth its own number one day; it is not what
# these shapes are for.
#
# These are CYRIUS baseline numbers, NOT comparable to
# rust-old/bench-history.csv. See CLAUDE.md.
#
# Stdlib is auto-prepended from cyrius.cyml — do NOT include stdlib modules.
# =========================================================================

